<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA - FOREIGN DEBT IN Q1 FALLS TO $265.35.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA - FOREIGN DEBT IN Q1 FALLS TO $265.35.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonia's foreign debt was $265.35 million in the first quarter compared to $271.54 in the previous quarter, the finance ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Foreign debt has decreased because part of an EBRD loan was paid back in February,&quot; Agate Dalton, international section head, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Dalton has said earlier that Estonia will not increase its foreign debt burden.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
